# 0008. Coverage: JaCoCo through AGP, aggregated at the root, 85% gate

Date: ${SCAFFOLD_DATE}
Status: Accepted

## Context

The gate needs one aggregated coverage number across Android and JVM modules, including Compose code
exercised by Robolectric screen tests.

Alternatives considered:
- **Kover** (0.9.11) — nicer DSL and annotation-based exclusions (`@Composable`, Hilt), and AGP 9 support
  since 0.9.4. Rejected for now: two open issues hit this stack. On AGP 9 with built-in Kotlin and the
  configuration cache, the plugin can take its pre-9 path and fail on the removed `applicationVariants`
  API ([kotlinx-kover#815](https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx-kover/issues/815)); and `koverVerify` can report
  a different coverage than the report in parallel multi-module builds
  ([#781](https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx-kover/issues/781), [#738](https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx-kover/issues/738)).
  A gate that fails at random costs more than path-pattern exclusions, above all in the autonomous loop.

## Decision

AGP's built-in JaCoCo (`enableUnitTestCoverage` on debug) in every Android module, the `jacoco` plugin on
JVM modules, and the root convention `android-forge.root` aggregating both: `./gradlew coverageVerify`
fails below **85% line coverage**, `./gradlew coverageReport` writes HTML/XML. Robolectric-loaded classes
are counted (`includeNoLocationClasses`). Exclusions are class-file patterns: generated code and wiring
(Compose singletons, serializers, Hilt modules, entry points, `api` modules, entry builders, design tokens).

## Consequences

- Easier: works on AGP 9 with built-in Kotlin today; screens covered by screen tests count.
- Harder: exclusions are path patterns, not annotations — a new kind of generated class may need a pattern;
  85% leaves little room, so new code ships with its tests. Revisit Kover (supersede this ADR) once
  #815 and #781 are closed.
